opt.system.language.label=Game language
opt.system.language.desc=The game's language: text and speech.
opt.launcher.language.label=Launcher language
opt.launcher.language.desc=The launcher's language. It is separate from the game's language.
opt.system.esc_quits.label=Esc closes the game
opt.system.esc_quits.desc=Esc is not a PS3 button; off leaves it free.
opt.system.save_backups.label=Save backups
opt.system.save_backups.desc=Copies kept of a save before the game writes over it.
opt.system.steady_audio.label=Steady audio
opt.system.steady_audio.desc=Runs the game's sound on a thread of its own, so heavy fights do not break it up.
opt.system.speakers.label=Speakers
opt.system.speakers.desc=Auto follows the output device; 7.1 for Windows Sonic or Dolby Atmos for Headphones. Surround also needs the game's Sound Mode (Options, Audio) on 5.1 or 7.1.
opt.system.raw_audio.label=Bypass sound effects
opt.system.raw_audio.desc=The game's sound skips Windows' and the sound card's effects (equalizers, loudness, virtual surround), where the device has a way past them.
opt.system.precompile_music.label=Precompile music
opt.system.precompile_music.desc=Music on the screen that builds the shaders at a version's first start, made by the program.
opt.launcher.show.label=Show this window at start
opt.launcher.show.desc=When off, hold Shift while the game starts to bring it back.
opt.launcher.update_check.label=Check for updates
opt.launcher.update_check.desc=At most every six hours, asks GitHub whether a newer release is out, and says so here with a link to it.
