opt.graphics.gpu.label=Graphics card
opt.graphics.vibrance.label=Colour vibrance
opt.graphics.vibrance.desc=Strength of the colour vibrance in the final picture.
opt.graphics.contrast.label=Contrast
opt.graphics.contrast.desc=Strength of the contrast in the final picture.
opt.graphics.shader_prebuild.label=Pixel shaders built ahead
opt.graphics.shader_prebuild.desc=Builds the pixel shaders before play, after the vertex shaders on the first start.
opt.graphics.render_scale.label=Internal resolution
opt.graphics.render_scale.desc=What the scene is drawn at. Bloom, blur and shadow maps stay at the game's size. FSR 3.1 and frame generation go no higher than the window.
opt.graphics.scaling.label=Scaling
opt.graphics.scaling.desc=How the picture is scaled to the window. FSR 3.1 builds the detail from past frames, in place of SMAA, and FSR 1 takes over where there is no scene.
opt.graphics.sharpening.label=FSR sharpening
opt.graphics.sharpening.desc=The sharpening pass of FSR (RCAS). Only with FSR scaling.
opt.graphics.frame_generation.label=Frame generation
opt.graphics.frame_generation.desc=FSR 3.1: twice the frames on screen, with VSync on. The game is held at half the monitor's refresh rate, 30 at 60 Hz and 60 at 120 Hz. A frame is made between each two, which holds the picture back by about a frame, and below 25 it stands aside.
opt.graphics.antialiasing.label=Anti-aliasing
opt.graphics.antialiasing.desc=Smooths jagged edges after the game has drawn the frame. Costs next to nothing. FSR 3.1 scaling does this itself in play.
opt.graphics.anisotropy.label=Anisotropic filtering
opt.graphics.anisotropy.desc=Sharper textures seen at an angle. The game itself asks for none.
opt.graphics.async_shaders.label=Build shaders in the background
opt.graphics.async_shaders.desc=A new shader is built while the game goes on, instead of a stall.
opt.graphics.render_thread.label=Render thread
opt.graphics.render_thread.desc=The GPU's work is recorded and shown on a thread of its own, beside the one that reads the game's commands: about 10% more frames where that one holds the game back.
opt.graphics.pipeline_wait.label=Build pipelines first
opt.graphics.pipeline_wait.desc=At the start the game waits until the pipelines kept from earlier sessions are built, so none is built while you play: a moment, a few seconds after a GPU driver update.
